\section{What do you have?}

\ltnote{%
  Relevant learning objectives: \cref{AiLOInstruct}.

  We ask this first because the rest of the session is pitched by the answer.
  If most of the room has only browser chat, the demonstration shows them
  something they can't yet do, and the exercises must not assume an agent.
  The options come from the course material on LLM tools and how to reach them,
  so that the same distinction between tool and access route carries over.
}%
Before we discuss what coding agents do to literate programming, we need to
know
what you have to work with.
Tick everything you could use today, whether or not you pay for it.

\begin{frame}[fragile]
  \begin{exercise}\label{ex:ai-tools}
\begin{pycode}
ai_poll(
